@tradition letters-evening
// Letters evening (weekly, seat 15). Sunday after the long table: the call-home booths for recorded messages, and the
// postbox by the booths for paper letters (Alejandro Reyes writes on paper), which go out with the next relay. People
// without a booth write at the bow lounge's tables. Quiet and warm. Design note: plans/trad-notes-weekly.md.
k: 441
title: Letters evening
when: weekly sunday
at: 19:15-20:15
min: 20
jitter: 15
where: 3 room Call-home booths: callhome, bench
where: 3 room Bow lounge: lounge-seat
hold: 1
who: reyes-alejandro always, calls-home 75%, quiet-corner 30%, everyone 10%
anim: calls-home none, everyone read
host: reyes-alejandro
from: ferreira
ties: decor postbox

== mail
- Letters evening tomorrow from {time}: the call-home booths are booked for crew, and the postbox goes out with the next relay. Paper and envelopes at the comms desk.   #warm

== ask
- Letters evening tonight. I owe my sister about six pages.   #funny
- I'm writing home later. It's been a while. Too long, probably.   #warm
- Letters evening after dinner. I never know how to start them.

== here
- How do you spell "hydroponics"? Never mind. "The garden".   #funny
- Dear everyone. The food is good. I miss you. That's most of it.   #warm
- Shh. I'm on the hard bit.

== thanks
- You sit down with the letter writers. For a while there's only the scratch of pens and someone's voice, low, in a booth.   #warm

== chatter
- I wrote home on Sunday. It'll take weeks to get there. I hope they like the drawing.   #warm
- Reyes writes real letters, on paper, in ink. Takes him all evening.
- The postbox is the only thing aboard that's slower than the lift.   #funny
